{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Have you not known.</b> By independent reasoning, which is the primary [method]." "<b>Have you not heard.</b> That others should teach it to them." "<b>Has it not been told you from the beginning.</b> And this is lower than all the [above] methods." "<b>From the beginning.</b> From the day you came into being, and if you have no knowledge, have you not understood the foundations of the earth?"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:11.209799943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}